From: RetroOPI_Z3
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: orangepi-zero3: CPU cooling map, 1512 MHz for speed grades 0/2

Bind cpu-thermal's passive trip to the CPUs (none was bound), raise the trips
to 80/90 C, and allow the 1512 MHz OPP for speed grades 0 and 2 at 1.10 V,
the voltage they already use at 1416 MHz and the vdd-cpu maximum.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts	2026-10-04 11:24:33.643464800 +0300
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts	2026-10-04 11:24:33.647464881 +0300
@@ -145,3 +145,45 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * RetroOPI_Z3: CPU thermal protection, and 1512 MHz for this board's speed grades.
+ *
+ * Thermal: the H616 dtsi defines cpu-thermal trips (60/70 C passive) but binds no
+ * cooling device, so nothing ever throttled; only the 110 C critical trip acted.
+ * Bind the CPUs to the first passive trip and raise both trips, so normal play
+ * (measured 58-65 C in Sonic Adventure 2) is never throttled, while a fan failure
+ * or an overclock that runs hot is.
+ *
+ * 1512 MHz: sun50i-h616-cpu-opp.dtsi offers it only to speed grades 1, 3 and 5
+ * (opp-supported-hw 0x2a, 1.10 V for 1 and 3). This Zero3's chip is grade 0 or 2:
+ * its available frequencies stop at 1416 MHz, which runs at 1.10 V, the vdd-cpu
+ * (dcdc2) maximum in this dts. Allow 1512 MHz for grades 0 and 2 at that SAME
+ * 1.10 V. This is an overclock for these grades, verified with a self-checking
+ * all-core stress test and in games (see DevelopmentLog). No voltage is raised.
+ */
+&cpu_threshold {
+	temperature = <80000>;
+};
+
+&cpu_target {
+	temperature = <90000>;
+};
+
+&{/thermal-zones/cpu-thermal} {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map0 {
+			trip = <&cpu_threshold>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu0 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>,
+					 <&cpu1 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>,
+					 <&cpu2 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>,
+					 <&cpu3 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&{/opp-table-cpu/opp-1512000000} {
+	opp-microvolt-speed0 = <1100000>;
+	opp-microvolt-speed2 = <1100000>;
+	opp-supported-hw = <0x2f>;
+};
